title: Names that match
intro: A trigger or counter that names an action or output nothing has is flagged, and a renamed action keeps answering to its old name.
project: Platformer | Names

chapter: A trigger doing something nothing can | Flagged in the Inspector
create: Empty
rename: Rules
add: Trigger
set: Trigger.Message = Boom
set: Trigger.Do = Explode
expectflagged: Trigger.Do = Explode
explain: field:Trigger.Do | Do | Nothing on this entity has an action called Explode, so the field is flagged. The same name is listed by scene_tree for agents, reported when the game is loaded and said in Output as it starts, instead of the trigger silently doing nothing.
set: Trigger.Do = Set Flag
set: Trigger.With = Rich
expectflagged: Trigger.Do = none
say: Naming an action Set Flag has resolves, so the flag goes away.

chapter: A counter reading what isn't there | Outputs the same way
select: Score
set: Counter.Track = Player
set: Counter.Output = Silver
expectflagged: Counter.Output = Silver
set: Counter.Output = Speed
expectflagged: Counter.Output = none
say: A script that renames an action or output with FormerName keeps every trigger, button, counter and wire that still names the old one working.
